Package: pushnav-headless
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: Arun Venkataswamy <5359196+arunvenkataswamy@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.36), libjpeg62-turbo, adduser
Section: science
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/meridianfield/pushnav
Description: PushNav plate-solving push-to for Raspberry Pi (headless)
 PushNav plate-solves live frames from a finder camera to show where a
 manual telescope is pointing and guide it to a target (push-to).
 .
 This is the headless Raspberry Pi build: it runs as a systemd service
 with no window, and is controlled from a phone or laptop browser at
 http://<pi-ip>:8765. SkySafari / Stellarium Mobile connect over LX200
 on port 4030, Stellarium desktop on port 10001.
 .
 It bundles its own Python 3.12 runtime under /usr/lib/pushnav-headless.
 For a PC or laptop, use the regular PushNav desktop release instead.
